DSA (Data Structures and Algorithms) is a fundamental area of computer science that focuses on how data is organized (data structures) and how problems are solved efficiently (algorithms). Together, they help write programs that are faster, use less memory, and scale to large inputs.
1. What is a Data Structure?
A data structure is a way of storing and organizing data so that operations like searching, inserting, deleting, and updating can be performed efficiently.
